; Deadlock detection, single thread: a lone main-context receiver on a
; channel with a live send handle (held by main itself, never used) can
; never make progress — no other thread exists to send, and the channel
; is not closed. The bounded channel wait detects that every live thread
; is blocked with no event in flight and traps exit 106 instead of
; hanging forever (the pre-fix behavior).
; ExpectedExit: 106

let page Page.allocate_page()
let sched Scheduler.create(page)
let ch Channel.create()
let raw Channel.receive(ch)
Console.println "unreachable"
Page.release_page(page)
